/// the behavior users expect when snapshotting a failing command
/// solely to show its diagnostic output.
///
/// With `skip` set, no child process is created and every command
/// is paired with empty output.  Otherwise `sh -c` is used so that
/// pipelines, redirections, and other shell syntax work as typed.
///
'''
